- op: discuss  # 52f0
  at: '2026-08-15T04:44:08Z'  # 52f0
  by: agent  # 52f0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 52f0
  clock: 5  # 52f0
  nonce: 52f0  # 52f0
  message: "MECHANISM FOUND AND REPRODUCED OUTSIDE CI. The stale-shared-site-packages\nhypothesis is DEAD, and it was not disproven by argument but by building the\ncontainer's environment and watching the failure appear.\n\nTHE DISCRIMINATOR, in a clean venv carrying exactly the four packages the\ntest-agent-infra step installs (pytest, pytest-xdist, pyyaml, hypothesis):\n\n  pytest tests/                                ->  2 failed, 1515 passed\n  pytest tests/test_rct_public_api_pinned.py   ->  8 failed, 1 passed\n\nSame tree, same interpreter, same install set. The only variable is which\nOTHER tests shared the worker. That single split explains every observation\nthis item was filed on.\n\nWHY. Fourteen scripts/check-* and generate-* helpers do\nsys.path.insert(0, <repo>/packages/hypergumbo-core/src) at MODULE level, and\nsibling tests execute them through SourceFileLoader. The insert lands in the\nshared interpreter, so the RCT pinning tests were importing hypergumbo_core\noff a path a sibling had put there. Whether they could import at all came\ndown to xdist sharding. The traceback in the CI log said so all along and I\nhad read past it: it names\npackages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/cli.py, which is the CHECKOUT,\nnot site-packages. There was never a stale package; there was never a shared\nvolume; the container needed nothing the workflow file fails to describe.\n\nTHE EARLIER 8-of-9 DISCREPANCY, which is what blocked this item for two\nsessions, was an artifact of the reconstruction: it ran that file ALONE.\nRunning it alone is the 8-failure arm. So the local reconstruction and CI\nnever disagreed - they were two different experiments.\n\nFIXED IN PR #349:\n  * tests/test_rct_public_api_pinned.py declares the one source root it\n    needs, so it behaves identically alone and in the suite.\n  * tests/test_rct_pinned_standalone.py re-runs it in a child interpreter\n    with the in-repo package roots scrubbed. The subprocess is load-bearing,\n    not ceremony: on a dev box every packages/*/src is a literal sys.path\n    entry from the editable install, so an in-process assertion would pass\n    with or without the fix - a discriminator not unique to the change.\n    Control: passes with the declaration, fails without it.\n  * rich and mypy added to the step, now for reasons rather than hope.\n    cli.py imports rich at module scope. The mypy-gate test's positive\n    control asserts the ratchet's exit 1 (regression), which is unreachable\n    at exit 2 (its documented infra failure when mypy is absent) - verified\n    in the same venv: with mypy present the ratchet returns 1 and prints\n    REGRESSION.\n\nSTATUS: pending_validation, NOT satisfied. The statement has two clauses.\n\"Reproducible outside CI\" is now SATISFIED, with the repro above and a\nCI-equivalent rerun of the whole step at 1518 passed, 0 failed. \"Green on\ndev\" is NOT yet evidenced - the cron fires at 0 1,13 UTC and the fix landed\nafter the 01:00 run. Closing on a local rerun would be exactly the proxy\nclosure the closure-evidence discipline forbids. Re-check with\n'ci-debug logs cron/full-suite <dev tip>' after the next cron.\n\nALSO CORRECTED, because it made this item unreadable: the cron IS firing on\nschedule and its two most recent runs are 7812c0b6a0 (08-14 13:00 UTC) and\n1de346d6d4 (08-15 01:00 UTC), both FAILURE. WI-zavut's note that \"no earlier\ncommit has a full-suite context at all\" is superseded."  # 52f0
- op: discuss  # 76ee
  at: '2026-08-17T22:02:51Z'  # 76ee
  by: agent  # 76ee
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 76ee
  clock: 6  # 76ee
  nonce: 76ee  # 76ee
  message: "P0/P1 SWEEP 2026-08-17, dev 11a240f83d. Every claim below was re-derived against the current tree, not re-read off this thread.\n\nSATISFIED. Both clauses now hold, and the second one is evidenced by the gate itself rather than by a local rerun -- which is what this item's own last entry said it was waiting for.\n\nTHE CRON IS GREEN AND HAS STAYED GREEN. Three consecutive full-suite cron runs on dev, after four consecutive failures:\n\n    7db9a5efb3  08-16 04:45   FAILURE\n    5aed26a8d1  08-16 13:40   FAILURE\n    8e913045e0  08-16 14:25   FAILURE\n    5a9e39f94f  08-16 15:02   FAILURE\n    8e69f40356  08-16 15:46   SUCCESS   <- transition\n    322a153915  08-16 20:21   SUCCESS\n    c36ad76be8  08-17 08:04   SUCCESS\n\nSAME STEP, NOT A PROXY. I fetched the cron/full-suite log at c36ad76be8 and checked the pip line this item quoted. It now reads:\n\n    + pip install pytest pytest-xdist pyyaml 'hypothesis~=6.100' rich 'mypy~=2.1.0'\n\n-- the same step, now carrying the two packages PR #349 added, with rich-15.0.0 and mypy-2.1.0 in the resolved install set. The run ends:\n\n    1530 passed, 2 skipped, 10 warnings in 16.17s\n\nagainst this item's filed  3 failed, 1498 passed, 2 skipped. Zero failures, and 31 MORE tests collected than at the filed SHA -- so this is not a green bought by collecting less.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT ESTABLISH, stated because the obvious reading is wrong. The green is NOT attributable to PR #349 alone: three of the four failures above POSTDATE it, and were closed by the meta-package install (8e913045e0) and the framework-patterns cache fix (8e69f40356, INV-kazij). What the evidence supports is this item's own statement -- the gate is green on dev, reproducibly, at the stage the defect lived -- not a causal claim about a single fix."  # 76ee
